+# Why the USDC balance was blank — the whole arc
+
+## TL;DR
+
+`useScaffoldReadContract` looks the contract up **by name** in a registry that
+Scaffold-ETH builds from two files. `USDC` was in neither, so the hook found no
+address/ABI, disabled the underlying wagmi query, and returned `undefined` —
+never firing a request, never throwing. The teammate pasted USDC into
+`deployedContracts.ts`, which is a **generated file** that `yarn deploy`
+overwrites from scratch, so the fix was destined to vanish. The correct home is
+`packages/nextjs/contracts/externalContracts.ts`, which the codegen never
+touches.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Why the hook returned `undefined` silently instead of erroring
+
+`useScaffoldReadContract` doesn't take an address. It takes a **contract name**
+and resolves it internally via `useDeployedContractInfo(contractName)`. That
+helper searches the merged `contracts` map (see part 3) for an entry matching
+`contractName` **on the currently connected chain**.
+
+For `"USDC"` there was no entry, so `deployedContractData` came back
+`undefined`. The hook then wires wagmi's `useReadContract` roughly like this:
+
+```ts
+useReadContract({
+  address: deployedContract?.address,
+  abi: deployedContract?.abi,
+  functionName,
+  args,
+  query: {
+    enabled: !!deployedContract && /* args ready */,
+  },
+});
+```
+
+With no contract data, `enabled` is `false`. A disabled wagmi query **never
+runs**:
+
+- no `address`/`abi` to call → nothing to send
+- `data` stays `undefined`
+- **no network request** (matches the empty network tab)
+- **no throw** — "contract not registered" is a soft/empty state in Scaffold-ETH,
+  not an exception
+
+So every observed symptom lines up: `undefined`, no error, no request.
+
+### "But shouldn't TypeScript have caught it?"
+
+`contractName` is typed as a union of the *registered* contract names. With USDC
+unregistered, `contractName: "USDC"` is technically a **type error**. It didn't
+stop anyone because the Next.js dev server doesn't hard-fail on TS type errors —
+it compiles and runs anyway. So the mistake surfaced only as a runtime
+`undefined`, which is exactly the quiet failure that's easy to chase for hours.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Why the teammate's fix worked all week, then self-destructed
+
+`packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts` is **auto-generated**. Its
+header literally says not to edit it by hand. It is produced by the deploy
+pipeline in the hardhat package: after `hardhat deploy` writes artifacts into
+`packages/hardhat/deployments/`, a post-deploy step (`generateTsAbis.ts`, run as
+part of `yarn deploy`) reads that `deployments/` folder and **overwrites
+`deployedContracts.ts` from scratch**.
+
+- Pasting USDC in by hand worked as long as nobody regenerated the file — the
+  registry now contained a `USDC` entry, so the hook resolved it. Fine all week.
+- `yarn deploy` regenerated the file **only from `deployments/`**. USDC is a
+  third-party Circle contract already live on Base — it was never deployed by
+  your hardhat project, so there's no `deployments/` artifact for it. The
+  regenerator had no knowledge of it and simply didn't emit it.
+
+Result: the hand-added entry was clobbered, USDC fell out of the registry, and
+the payouts page went blank again. The fix wasn't wrong data — it was in a file
+owned by a machine.
+
+---
+
+## 3. The correct registration
+
+Scaffold-ETH merges **two** sources into the contract registry the hooks read:
+
+| File | Owner | Purpose |
+|------|-------|---------|
+| `contracts/deployedContracts.ts` | **generated** by `yarn deploy` | contracts *your* hardhat project deploys |
+| `contracts/externalContracts.ts` | **you, by hand** | contracts you *don't* deploy (tokens, protocols, anything already on-chain) |
+
+`externalContracts.ts` is never touched by the codegen, so entries there survive
+every `yarn deploy`. USDC on Base belongs here.
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/contracts/externalContracts.ts`
+
+```ts
+import { GenericContractsDeclaration } from "~~/utils/scaffold-eth/contract";
+
+/**
+ * @example
+ * const externalContracts = {
+ *   1: {
+ *     DAI: { address: "0x...", abi: [...] },
+ *   },
+ * } as const;
+ */
+const externalContracts = {
+  // Base mainnet — chain id 8453
+  8453: {
+    USDC: {
+      // Native Circle USDC on Base
+      address: "0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913",
+      abi: [
+        {
+          type: "function",
+          name: "balanceOf",
+          stateMutability: "view",
+          inputs: [{ name: "account", type: "address" }],
+          outputs: [{ name: "", type: "uint256" }],
+        },
+        {
+          type: "function",
+          name: "decimals",
+          stateMutability: "view",
+          inputs: [],
+          outputs: [{ name: "", type: "uint8" }],
+        },
+        {
+          type: "function",
+          name: "symbol",
+          stateMutability: "view",
+          inputs: [],
+          outputs: [{ name: "", type: "string" }],
+        },
+        {
+          type: "function",
+          name: "transfer",
+          stateMutability: "nonpayable",
+          inputs: [
+            { name: "to", type: "address" },
+            { name: "amount", type: "uint256" },
+          ],
+          outputs: [{ name: "", type: "bool" }],
+        },
+        {
+          type: "function",
+          name: "approve",
+          stateMutability: "nonpayable",
+          inputs: [
+            { name: "spender", type: "address" },
+            { name: "amount", type: "uint256" },
+          ],
+          outputs: [{ name: "", type: "bool" }],
+        },
+        {
+          type: "function",
+          name: "allowance",
+          stateMutability: "view",
+          inputs: [
+            { name: "owner", type: "address" },
+            { name: "spender", type: "address" },
+          ],
+          outputs: [{ name: "", type: "uint256" }],
+        },
+      ],
+    },
+  },
+} as const;
+
+export default externalContracts satisfies GenericContractsDeclaration;
+```
+
+### Key details
+
+- **Chain id `8453`** = Base mainnet. The outer key must match the chain the app
+  is connected to, or `useDeployedContractInfo` won't find USDC on that chain and
+  you're back to `undefined`. If you also run against a fork/other network, add
+  those chain ids too.
+- **Address `0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913`** is **native USDC**
+  (Circle) on Base. Do *not* confuse it with the older bridged **USDbC**
+  (`0xd9aAEc86B65D86f6A7B5B1b0c42FFA531710b6CA`) — different token, different
+  balance.
+- **ABI** only needs the functions you call. `balanceOf` is enough for the
+  payouts read; the rest above (`decimals`, `transfer`, `approve`, `allowance`,
+  `symbol`) are the usual ERC-20 surface you'll want next and give you full type
+  inference on args/returns.
+- `as const` + `satisfies GenericContractsDeclaration` is what gives the hooks
+  their literal types, so `contractName: "USDC"` and `functionName: "balanceOf"`
+  become valid and fully typed — the original TS error disappears for the right
+  reason.
+- USDC uses **6 decimals**, so format the returned `uint256` with `formatUnits(x, 6)`,
+  not `formatEther`.
+
+Once USDC lives in `externalContracts.ts`, it's part of the registry on every
+build, it survives `yarn deploy`, and the payouts page reads the balance
+reliably.

